                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've been following this game ever since I saw one of RGCD's early videos on YouTube, while he was also working on an OUYA version. As soon as this game came out, I tried to get it asap, while waiting for this Steam version to come out. The developer kindly gave a Steam key for people who purchased it out of Steam, but I wouldn't mind purchasing it again.\n\nThe game's premise is simple, but challenging: you control your conganoid with your left stick, which \"stretches\" its tail and uses it to hit mobs and score the most. Some mobs charge your lazor, you must close mob-spawning portals, there are some invincible mobs and you must reach a certain kill count before advancing!\n\nWhen you see the videos, it looks pretty simple and easy to play, which isn't far-off. The game itself it really simple to learn, but mastering and prolonging your gameplay's another story.\n\nReally fun, addicting and challenging! For those who like arena-based games, it's really fun to play and the feeling is also great too. It's short, but has a great replay factor, which makes it a great game for short breaks (though I sometimes play it for a tad more ;D).\n\nAlso, it has a great soundtrack, which makes the game even more worth playing! :)",
